SOAPBOX: Rough conditions for a little pistol on 160 on SSB. Lots of storm
SOAPBOX: noise here Friday night, and I could not even work stations I normally
SOAPBOX: can on SSB. Played in the NAQP RTTY contest Saturday night and then
SOAPBOX: checked into 160 after midnight. Noise level down, but still struggled
SOAPBOX: to work stations. I also heard many other stations calling others with
SOAPBOX: no responses. ZF is usually a slam dunk for me from middle TN with LP
SOAPBOX: and a compromise antenna. ZF2VE was 20 over S9 here Sunday morning
SOAPBOX: just after midnight, and I was unable to get his attention. Neither
SOAPBOX: could a host of other ops calling him. The path from my location to
SOAPBOX: VE3 was the only solid path as I worked all the VE3s I heard with no
SOAPBOX: problems! Very strange conditions.
SOAPBOX: 73, Gene N9TF, Rig K3S 100 watts to 22' vertical to knee inverted L
SOAPBOX: 110' horizontal wire traveling west from vertical radiator.
